<worksheet>
    <title>LT3-4:Linear Patterns and Equations</title>
    <subtitle>Beginning Algebra Made Useful by Char E. Beckman</subtitle>
    <page>
    <exercise workspace="yes">
        <introduction>
            <p>
                 What do you know about linear equations? Give brief answers now and think about these questions as you work on the problems below.</p>
             
        </introduction>       
    <task workspace="yes">
        <p>
            What patterns would you see in a table of data that can be modeled by a linear equation?
        </p>
    </task>
    <task workspace="yes">
        <p>
            What patterns would you see in a graph of data that can be modeled by a linear equation?
        </p>
    </task>
    <task workspace="yes">
        <p>How can you tell a graph can be modeled by a linear equation?
        </p> 
    </task>
    <task workspace="yes">
        <p>What would an equation of a linear equation look like?</p>
    </task>
</exercise>
